# __NAME__

A [rustango-cms](https://github.com/ujeenet/rustango-cms) site, generated with `rcms new`.

## Run (SQLite — no database server)

SQLite has no schemas, so each tenant lives in its own file: use
**database-mode** tenancy (`--mode database`) with an explicit
`--host-pattern` so requests can be routed to the tenant.

```sh
export DATABASE_URL="sqlite:./var/registry.db?mode=rwc"
ARGS="--no-default-features --features sqlite"

cargo run $ARGS -- migrate-registry     # create the registry (orgs, …)
cargo run $ARGS -- create-tenant demo \
    --mode database \
    --database-url "sqlite:./var/demo.db?mode=rwc" \
    --host-pattern demo.localhost       # database mode needs an explicit host
cargo run $ARGS -- create-superuser demo admin   # you need this to sign in
cargo run $ARGS -- runserver
```

- Sign in: <http://demo.localhost:8080/login>
- Admin: <http://demo.localhost:8080/cms-admin/pages>
- Public pages: `http://demo.localhost:8080/<slug>/`
- Sitemap: <http://demo.localhost:8080/sitemap.xml>

`create-tenant` applies the tenant migrations for you, so there's no separate
`migrate-tenants` step on a fresh install.

## Run (PostgreSQL)

Same order, minus the SQLite-specific flags:

```sh
createdb __NAME__
export DATABASE_URL=postgres://localhost/__NAME__
export RUSTANGO_APEX_DOMAIN=localtest.me   # tenant host = demo.localtest.me

cargo run -- migrate-registry
cargo run -- create-tenant demo
cargo run -- create-superuser demo admin
cargo run -- runserver
```

- Sign in: <http://demo.localtest.me:8080/login>
- Admin: <http://demo.localtest.me:8080/cms-admin/pages>
